    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Hodson Bay, An exceptional site measuring approximately 3.311 acres, located in the highly sought-after area of Hodson Bay, with planning for the construction of five detached luxury homes, offering a unique opportunity for developers or investors. Given its scale and location, the site may also be suitable for a higher density scheme, subject to the necessary planning permission.\n\nSituated in a picturesque and tranquil setting, this site combines scenic surroundings with excellent development potential. Don't miss the chance to create a premium residential enclave in this prime location.\n\nHodson Bay, located just outside Athlone, is a picturesque and tranquil area known for its stunning natural beauty and close proximity to Lough Ree. This sought-after location offers a perfect blend of peaceful countryside living with easy access to Athlone town's amenities, including schools, shopping, and dining options. The area is a haven for outdoor enthusiasts, with boating, fishing, and scenic walking trails readily available. Hodson Bay is also home to the renowned Hodson Bay Hotel and golf courses, making it a desirable location for those seeking a balanced lifestyle of both relaxation and recreation. Its idyllic charm and connectivity make Hodson Bay a prime residential location."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Approx. 3.311 Acres\nFolio RN15141F\nFull Planning Permission for 5 Detached Luxury Homes\nPrestigious Hodson Bay Location\nDevelopment Opportunity\nPotential for Higher Density Scheme (S.P.P.)\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "BER Details",
        "SortOrder": 4,
        "Content": "BER Exempt\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Directions",
        "SortOrder": 5,
        "Content": "Located in Barrymore, Hodson Bay, just minutes from Athlone town centre, Hodson Bay Hotel and Lough Ree."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Negotiator",
        "SortOrder": 10,
        "Content": "Cormac Sheehy"
      }
